errors.Is against a sentinel matched through a custom Is method: NotFoundError[ID].Is(ErrNotFound) is true,
so "not found" never leaves Exists (Go semantics: no NotFoundError entry).
Custom Is methods are may-match in v1, so expect NotFoundError[AccountID] kept and marked possibly handled;
remaining: ctx.Err() (memory), read errors behind "filerepo: read %s: %w", decode errors behind CorruptError.Unwrap.
